rd-suggestion","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":213994,"global_rank":252873,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":39987},{"name":"vburca/MeshHoles","owner":"vburca","html_url":"https://github.com/vburca/MeshHoles","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":1,"language":"Python","description":"Outline holes within a triangular mesh","topics":[],"score":213994,"global_rank":252882,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":39988},{"name":"shanebrewer/Starcraft_2_AI","owner":"shanebrewer","html_url":"https://github.com/shanebrewer/Starcraft_2_AI","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Basic AI for Starcraft II","topics":[],"score":213991,"global_rank":252914,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":39989},{"name":"ahmedhamdy2121/Deep-Learning-Neural-Network","owner":"ahmedhamdy2121","html_url":"https://github.com/ahmedhamdy2121/Deep-Learning-Neural-Network","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"My tests on the neural network and deep learning in Python","topics":["deep-learning","keras","neural-network","python","tensorflow"],"score":213991,"global_rank":252919,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":39990},{"name":"lakshadvani/FaultToleranceRaft","owner":"lakshadvani","html_url":"https://gith